<title>PERU: Peru int'l reserves rise to $9.410 bln end-April.</title>
<headline>Peru int'l reserves rise to $9.410 bln end-April.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-05-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's Central Reserve Bank said Saturday its net international reserves rose to $9.410 billion by the end of April, up $237 million from the close of March.</p>
<p>Peru's reserves, which have recovered steadily since President Alberto Fujimori's government took power in 1990, ended 1996 at $8.540 billion.</p>
<p>((-- Lima Newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
